y}.","15334":"Publish canteen menu was modified","15335":"Non-exercising","15336":"No smartwatches paired with this device found","15337":"Available","15338":"Make available","15339":"Revoke access","15340":"Not available","15341":"Send \/ make documents available via EduPage","15342":"Documents have been sent and made available","15343":"Access to documents has been revoked.","15344":"Decisions and documents can be made available to parents and teachers electronically via EduPage.\r\nUsers are notified when a document becomes available and can view or download it. The system also records whether the document has been downloaded.","15345":"Question types","15346":"Generate only these types of questions","15347":"Pedagogical","15348":"Organizational","15349":"School data","15350":"Assigned materials","15351":"Classification method","15352":"Last sent","15353":"Last sent for lost item","15354":"Send a notification about an item:","15355":"Send a Lost and Found alert","15356":"This lost item opens when you click on the message","15357":"Clicking on the message will open the Lost and Found module.","15358":"Categories of books changed","15359":"Do you want to change categories of {num} book titles?","15360":"Hide password","15361":"Extended on date","15362":"Extend","15363":"Extend the period for book return","15364":"EduPage suspects that your password may have been published or predictable. As a precaution, EduPage has reset your password, you can reset it via the \u201cI don\u2019t know my password\u201d link. EduPage was not hacked, the password was either too simple, commonly used, or you used it in another service where it was not sufficiently protected. Do not give your EduPage password to anyone, do not send it, or enter it in a service other than EduPage.","15365":"EduPage Malware Protection Service suspects that the password of user {username} may have been published or predictable. The password has been reset as a precaution. For more information and further 